{
    "word": "acicular",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0e05fda4-04d2-3c77-81e1-efa5f827f803",
                "word": "acicular",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "77e5cf70-dec4-3145-bc38-b440c97c0f4a",
                        "entry_id": "0e05fda4-04d2-3c77-81e1-efa5f827f803",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Needle-shaped; slender like a needle or bristle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d439df58-3666-42eb-8c82-9aac62c50358",
                                "sense_id": "77e5cf70-dec4-3145-bc38-b440c97c0f4a",
                                "text": "Near-synonyms: needlelike, pinlike"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2b6bb75-42ca-4710-9ee6-f1f26edf0d95",
                                "sense_id": "77e5cf70-dec4-3145-bc38-b440c97c0f4a",
                                "text": "1992, Oliver Sacks, Migraine, Berkeley: University of California Press, revised and expanded edition, Part 5, Chapter 17, p. 279,\nSometimes these networks have an acicular or crystalline appearance, and may grow visibly, sometimes with sudden jerks, “like frost on a windowpane,” or “primitive plants.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "164cffe1-5666-3ad5-ac7e-938381a82f29",
                        "entry_id": "0e05fda4-04d2-3c77-81e1-efa5f827f803",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having sharp points like needles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7bdd9d9d-544e-31d9-bb5e-7236ee19772d",
                        "entry_id": "0e05fda4-04d2-3c77-81e1-efa5f827f803",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a leaf, slender and pointed, needle-like."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f62f625-e735-46f0-be37-0b3c5fded1cf",
                                "sense_id": "7bdd9d9d-544e-31d9-bb5e-7236ee19772d",
                                "text": "the acicular foliage of coniferous trees"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6dcc5117-5280-49c9-9a10-536d1b1db5ed",
                                "sense_id": "7bdd9d9d-544e-31d9-bb5e-7236ee19772d",
                                "text": "[…] though fond of foliage, their trees always had a tendency to congeal into little acicular thorn-hedges, and never tossed free."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aaf8c5eb-59cf-45e2-974b-9c7951004790",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e05fda4-04d2-3c77-81e1-efa5f827f803",
                        "source_sense_description": "needle-shaped",
                        "target_lang_word": "aciculaire",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aciculaire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a725f462-ce76-32f9-99e0-a283bcccef42",
                                        "entry_id": "cedfbd63-e87f-3dd5-9b10-9f4ce9fecd7c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Se dit d’une feuille linéaire, rigide et pointue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01caf1cd-e411-4dce-9d34-da6e94cab93c",
                                                "sense_id": "a725f462-ce76-32f9-99e0-a283bcccef42",
                                                "text": "Au cours d’un contrôle je me rendis compte que la récolte était abondante et qu’elle venait du bois ; la chaleur et l’humidité, dans de bonnes proportions, avaient favorisé le phénomène du miellat sur les arbres : une sécrétion particulière qui suinte sur les feuilles aciculaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6673eea8-3c4d-4c90-b673-6644b31f72bd",
                                                "sense_id": "a725f462-ce76-32f9-99e0-a283bcccef42",
                                                "text": "Chez notre Pin, le cône végétatif d’un bourgeon à feuille aciculaire double n’est que très-faiblement développé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6716c399-820b-4ed6-a192-c192d18e205a",
                                                "sense_id": "a725f462-ce76-32f9-99e0-a283bcccef42",
                                                "text": "Les aiguilles des conifères sont des feuilles aciculaires."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "118475f0-2300-3522-8779-cd0e8c745286",
                                        "entry_id": "cedfbd63-e87f-3dd5-9b10-9f4ce9fecd7c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En forme de pointe très fine comme celle d’une aiguille ; c’est ce qu’on dit parfois du dernier article des palpes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88c1ec6e-f36a-3217-98bd-c52b920d8855",
                                        "entry_id": "cedfbd63-e87f-3dd5-9b10-9f4ce9fecd7c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En aiguilles ou en baguettes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92f916a7-babf-4b50-ba2a-3e3b7f216c8c",
                                                "sense_id": "88c1ec6e-f36a-3217-98bd-c52b920d8855",
                                                "text": "Le faciès aciculaire de certains silicates"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
